// expect: trap
// The main thread handles an inbox's messages, so an ask from it would wait for itself for ever: it
// stops the program instead. A send from the main thread is fine, and its answer comes with the
// next `handlePosted`.
import ui.{handlePosted, inbox}

main()
    val doubled = inbox((n: int) -> n * 2)
    val f = doubled.send(21)
    println(handlePosted())
    println(f.await())
    println(doubled.ask(1))
